  "title": "Fed Chair Warsh Stresses Price Stability Amid Rate Hike Uncertainty",
  "summary": "Federal Reserve Chairman Kevin Warsh stressed the importance of maintaining price stability, while offering no signals on interest rate adjustments during a meeting in October. The Fed raised its key interest rate by a quarter-point in September, but the outcome remained uncertain due to inflation expectations.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Federal Reserve Chairman Kevin Warsh did not prejudge what the US central bank will do about interest rates at its upcoming meetings in October and December.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The Fed increased its key interest rate by a quarter-point in September, its first increase in three years, and inflation will likely lead to another rate hike in coming months.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Warsh offered no fresh signals during a 'fireside chat' with International Monetary Fund Managing Director Kristalina Georgieva at a meeting of financial leaders in Bangkok.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
